// The village's buildings (worldgen structures::village lays them in a row
// on the plain beside the spawn, in this order, as many as fit). One
// character is one block (6 × 6 cells); the bottom row is the floor, set on
// the ground (brick foundations go down under it where the ground dips).
//
// ' ' the land as it is · '#' planks · '%' brick · '.' open, planks behind
// · ',' open to the sky (a window) · '-' a platform · 'W' water
// Doors: the lowest five rows open at both ends (the village is walked
// through, side on; a person is four blocks tall).
// Who lives or works there, standing on that block: g guide, s smith,
// h healer, m merchant. What stands there: A anvil, F furnace, B workbench.

